{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialShadowRigidity"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.keystone_q0_step_is_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.keystone_q0_step_is_free","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L103-L113","doc":"The keystone reading, with the substrate anchor named. `q₀` enters only as a\npoint at which both denominators are nonzero — an explicit, checkable side\ncondition on the concrete polynomials, not an assumption about `q₀` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.eq_of_rational_and_agree_on_rootsOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.eq_of_rational_and_agree_on_rootsOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L79-L101","doc":"**The reduction.** Two functions with rational presentations whose\ndenominators are nonvanishing on the roots of unity, and which agree at every\nroot of unity, agree at **every** point where both denominators are nonzero — the\nsubstrate anchor `q₀` included.\n\nThe archimedean step is therefore not an extra obligation: it is a consequence of\nthe root-of-unity match together with rationality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.eq_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.eq_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L77-L77","doc":"`F` agrees with `num/den` away from the zeros of `den`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.den","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.den","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Denominator polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.num","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Numerator polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.RationalPresentation","kind":"structure","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRootsOfUnityReduction.lean#L68-L77","doc":"`F` is presented as the rational function `num/den` wherever `den` does not\nvanish. This is data supplied by the caller, not an assertion that any particular\nobject admits such a presentation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}